  "cast": {
    "MAN": {"character": "the dragon", "model": "en_US-hfc_male-medium", "speaker_id": null, "length_scale": 1.05, "noise_scale": 0.667, "noise_w": 0.8, "median_f0": 116.6, "notes": "US male (HiFi-Captain). Best of 26 male candidates rendered on 11 of his lines: median F0 ~117 Hz (target 95-125), the most expressive of the field (F0 SD 4.1 st, not monotone), clearest diction (Whisper: 0 word errors, best mean log-prob -0.07) and best DNSMOS OVRL 3.43; perceived age ~34. Dialogue length_scale 1.05. Scene-8 voice-over (vo=true, fx='vo': intimate, a touch of room reverb) is slower: s8_l1 1.12, s8_l2 1.30, s8_l3 1.2 read as 'All it took was... / somebody to break it.' with a 0.40 s reflective pause (audit: the single-phrase take was the fastest VO line at 4.6 syl/s and opened on a declamatory ~210 Hz 'ALL'; the VO now runs ~3.1-3.5 syl/s overall, peaks ~165 Hz, accents land on 'somebody' / 'break'). Bright-ish timbre: a gentle -2 dB shelf above ~5 kHz warms the dragon in the mix. s4_l1 (fx='drowned') is cut off on purpose mid-breath ('Lately I f-'); the tavern music swells from beat s4_swell to bury it. s6_laugh is five 'hah' pulses of this same voice assembled into a real laugh bout (~1.2 s, pitch stepping down from ~196 to ~146 Hz, decrescendo): keep it MODERATE in the mix, about -3 to -4 dB under his dialogue level, never louder than the lines around it."},
    "PHARMACIST": {"character": "the lioness", "model": "en_US-libritts_r-medium", "speaker_id": 515, "length_scale": 1.06, "noise_scale": 0.5, "noise_w": 0.6, "median_f0": 186.0, "notes": "LibriTTS-R reader 5139. Soft and warm: dark timbre (spectral centroid ~300 Hz, LTAS tilt -10.8 dB/oct) with soft, breathy phonation (H1-H2 +7.4 dB), median F0 ~186-196 Hz, perceived age ~30, kind contour (F0 SD ~3 st). The only soft LibriTTS voice that never turned 'Try these' into 'Fry these' (6/6 Whisper-perfect renditions vs 3-4/6). Distinct from the gnome by timbre and age rather than pitch (darker and smoother: centroid ~300 vs ~420 Hz, breathy-soft vs rough, perceived ~30 vs ~54; they never share a scene) and from the stone (far less pitch movement, darker). length_scale 1.06, noise 0.5/0.6."},
    "PHONE": {"character": "the speaking stone", "model": "en_US-lessac-high", "speaker_id": null, "length_scale": 1.0, "noise_scale": 0.5, "noise_w": 0.5, "median_f0": 182.8, "notes": "US announcer-style female (high quality): crisp, very articulate menu voice (Whisper 0 errors, log-prob -0.08, DNSMOS 3.47), bright sing-song IVR contour (F0 SD ~5.8 st), median F0 ~183 Hz. noise 0.5/0.5 for a controlled, regular read. Captions off (scene 3 shows its words as glowing rune-text). Mix fx='phone': stone-phone band-pass (~300-3400 Hz) plus a faint magical shimmer; that, its pitch movement and brightness keep it well apart from the pharmacist."},
    "BOUNCER": {"character": "the stone troll", "model": "en_GB-vctk-medium", "speaker_id": 102, "length_scale": 1.35, "noise_scale": 0.5, "noise_w": 0.6, "median_f0": 76.0, "notes": "VCTK speaker p237 (Scottish male). The deepest + flattest combination of 26 male candidates: median F0 ~76 Hz (the lowest voice in the cast), F0 span ~4.8 st (a flat, bored monotone), dark timbre (centroid ~210 Hz). length_scale 1.35 (audit; was 1.18 = 4.0 syl/s, barely slower than the dragon): ~3.3 syl/s, 'Keep it light, [comma pause] buddy.' Take chosen for intelligibility under the tavern din: Whisper small+base hear it perfectly in 24/24 trials with pink noise at 20/12 dB SNR, -12 dB level and a 300-3400 Hz band-limit (the 1.18 take: 14/24, 'light' -> 'like' in noise); most seeds at >= 1.3 are misheard, so re-seed only with that check. noise 0.5/0.6."},
    "CROWD": {"character": "the pixie", "model": "en_US-libritts_r-medium", "speaker_id": 448, "length_scale": 0.92, "noise_scale": 0.5, "noise_w": 0.6, "median_f0": 266.0, "notes": "LibriTTS-R reader 4807: young (perceived ~27), high (median F0 ~250 Hz -- a tiny pixie), quick (fastest finalist, ~5.8 syl/s) and expressive (F0 SD ~3.9 st) for the sneer. 'Ew.' is fed as 'Eew!' (/ˈiːw!/, length_scale 1.0 for that word): espeak reads 'Ew.'/'Eww.' as /juː/ = 'you'. The exclamation gives a longer, higher [i] onset, the cue that separates 'ew' from 'you': the chosen take is heard as 'Ew' in 24/24 Whisper small+base trials (clean, noise 20/12 dB SNR, -12 dB, band-limited); the earlier 'Eew.' take was heard as 'You' by base.en in all 12 of its trials. length_scale 0.92, noise 0.5/0.6."},
    "OLD_WOMAN": {"character": "the gnome grandmother", "model": "en_US-libritts_r-medium", "speaker_id": 510, "length_scale": 1.24, "noise_scale": 0.5, "noise_w": 0.6, "median_f0": 173.3, "notes": "LibriTTS-R reader 4800: the oldest-sounding clean female voice found (perceived age ~54 after an age scan of all ~600 female-pitched LibriTTS-R/VCTK speakers; several 'older' candidates were high-pitched men and were rejected). Median F0 ~170-176 Hz (target 160-200); warm and twinkly (F0 SD ~3.9 st), the roughest/breathiest phonation of the finalists (HNR ~10 dB, the most F0 micro-perturbation -- an older voice quality), Whisper-perfect on 15/15 renditions. length_scale 1.24 (s6_l1 / s7_l3 takes at 1.30), noise 0.5/0.6: SPEC wants her 'slower pace, dry wit' -- at 1.15 she measured 4.3 syl/s, no slower than the lioness (4.2); now ~4.0 (punchline s6_l4 3.97, s7_l3 3.6), perceived age 47-54 vs the lioness's 32. 'I got the cat.' is fed as [[aɪ ɡˈɑːt ðə kæt.]] so the accent falls on GOT ('cat' is given information): 'They TOLD me to get a cat. I GOT the cat.' Spectrally the lioness is the darker voice (alpha ratio -22 vs ~-13 dB); for more warmth on the gnome use a gentle -2 dB shelf above ~3.5 kHz in the mix, never more (her consonant clarity carries the jokes)."},
